/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
39.6850393700787407 712.9136220472440755 Td
(LunarSafe is an autonomous, flight-grade lunar hazard assessment software suite engineered to guarantee) Tj
T* (deterministic hazard identification for lunar descent landers. Designed to run on uncalibrated and calibrated) Tj
T* (selenographic data from NASA LOLA DEM and ISRO Chandrayaan-2 TMC-2 sensors, the software eliminates) Tj
T* (stochastic variability across flight computers. By coupling Horn's 3D finite-difference slope model with) Tj
T* (morphological Sobel hazard segmenters, the system classifies 24m landing cells in under 2.5 seconds with) Tj
T* (zero floating-point divergence.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
39.6850393700787407 633.5435433070865656 Td
(2. Problem Statement: The Terminal Landing Hazard Dilemma) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
39.6850393700787407 620.7876377952754865 Td
(Lunar surface operations face extreme topography, where undetected craters \(>1.5m depth\), boulders) Tj
T* (\(>0.5m height\), or local slopes \(>10∞\) can cause lander tip-over, leg rupture, or thruster plume backfire.) Tj
T* (During the Chandrayaan-2 Vikram mission, terminal descent control challenges underscored the paramount) Tj
T* (requirement for ultra-fast, robust, deterministic landing site evaluation. While Chandrayaan-3 successfully) Tj
T* (utilized an expanded target zone \(4.0 km ◊ 2.4 km\) at Shiv Shakti Point, future exploration of the permanently) Tj
T* (shadowed craters of the lunar south pole demands real-time, reproducible hazard classification capable of) Tj
T* (evaluating terrain with high precision without relying on stochastic neural models that exhibit) Tj
T* (non-deterministic drift.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
11.5 TL
